From d11642c971134afc118b577e6406d5d44ee33c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 06:46:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] ##arch: USSE register profile, op metadata, ESIL

Add r2 analysis depth for the usse arch, layered on the unchanged,
byte-identical text decoder:
- register profile (regs.h): r0-63, pa/sa/o/c/g0-31, i0-15, drc0-1, pc,
  pclink, p0-3 -> r2 is register-aware (drp, reg tracking).
- op metadata: op->val (immediates; enables r2 ASCII hints), op->direction
  (ldad=READ / stad=WRITE), plus the existing type + branch jump/fail.
- ESIL for the scalar control subset (mov, and/or/xor, shl/shr, ldad/stad
  with dword->byte scaling, ba/br/ba.savelink, predicate-wrapped) so
  emulation (aae/aes) resolves computed addresses and updates registers.
- pseudo-C: ldad/stad -> mem[...], imae -> a * b + c.

Disassembly text is unchanged: 21/21 test/db/asm/usse pass, ukernel
byte-identical. SIMD/flagged forms (fmad/imae vectors, .test*, MOE) carry
no ESIL by design.
---
